---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { META, leaderboard } from '../lib/data';
import { CITE_ONLY, LICENSING_CREDITS } from '../data/credits';

const board = leaderboard();
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="What the Human Obsolescence Index is, how it stays honest, and who supplies the data.">
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 md:px-6">
    <p class="term-label text-phosphor">Prospectus disclosures</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl font-extrabold uppercase tracking-tight">About</h1>

    <section class="mt-8" aria-labelledby="what-title">
      <h2 id="what-title" class="font-display text-xl font-bold uppercase">What this is</h2>
      <div class="prose-block mt-3 space-y-3">
        <p>
          A stock exchange for human worth. The Human Obsolescence Index lists {board.length} U.S. occupations like
          securities and prices each one by how much of its work AI can touch and how its government-projected employment
          growth compares with every other occupation's. A high price is a ranking, not a forecast that the job shrinks or
          stops hiring. The ticker is a joke. The numbers are not.
        </p>
        <p>
          Each occupation gets a page with its score, the parts that make it up, what the job actually involves, and
          related jobs that BLS projects to grow. The {META.edition} edition uses data retrieved on {META.dataAsOf}; it is
          re-run every quarter (see the <a class="underline" href="/changelog/">changelog</a>).
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10" aria-labelledby="honesty-title" id="honesty">
      <h2 id="honesty-title" class="font-display text-xl font-bold uppercase">Gallows humor, with receipts</h2>
      <div class="prose-block mt-3 space-y-3">
        <p>
          We make jokes about the end of work because the alternative is pretending to be calm about it. The jokes stay in
          the headlines. Everything underneath is sourced.
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>Every number on this site comes from a public dataset named in the <a class="underline" href="/methodology/#sources">source manifest</a>, with its retrieval date and file hash.</li>
          <li>Exposure is not job loss. We say it on every occupation page, and BLS and Microsoft say it about their own data.</li>
          <li>The official BLS category always sits next to our score, labeled as BLS's, so you can see where we agree and where we don't.</li>
          <li>Missing data gets a visible flag, never a guess.</li>
          <li>The formula and weights are public. If you think they are wrong, you can recompute everything from the stat pack.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Punch hard, land helpful: every page ends with roles that are still growing.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10" aria-labelledby="licensing-title" id="licensing">
      <h2 id="licensing-title" class="font-display text-xl font-bold uppercase">Licensing and credits</h2>
      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3" data-credits>
        {
          LICENSING_CREDITS.map((c) => (
            <li class="panel p-4 [overflow-wrap:anywhere]" data-credit={c.id}>
              <p class="font-semibold">{c.who}</p>
              <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-dim">{c.what}</p>
              <p class="term-label mt-2">License: <a class="underline" href={c.url}>{c.license}</a></p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
      <p class="prose-block mt-4 text-dim">
        O*NET® is a trademark of USDOL/ETA. Our derived composite scores are released under CC BY 4.0; please credit the
        Human Obsolescence Index. Cited but never used as data: the Stanford Digital Economy Lab "Canaries" study (linked on
        the <a class="underline" href="/methodology/#reality-check">methodology page</a>).
      </p>
      <h3 class="term-label mt-6 text-amber">Cited, never used as data</h3>
      <p class="prose-block mt-2 text-dim">
        These are copyrighted or proprietary. We link to them as labeled citations only; none of their data is an input to
        any score, and none of it is redistributed.
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-3 space-y-1.5 text-sm [overflow-wrap:anywhere]" data-cite-only-list>
        {
          CITE_ONLY.map((c) => (
            <li>
              <a class="underline" href={c.url} rel="noopener" data-cite-only>{c.name}</a>
              <span class="text-amber"> · cite-only</span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
